# Layout

Each component lives at `components/<name>/`:

- `__init__.py` — package entry; usually re-exports the platform module (`from .sensor import *`, `from .climate import *`, etc.)
- `<platform>.py` — Python codegen and `CONFIG_SCHEMA` (`sensor.py`, `climate.py`, ...)
- `<name>.h` / `<name>.cpp` — C++ implementation in `namespace esphome::<name>`

# Codegen conventions

- Declare config keys as module-level `CONF_*` constants.
- Use `cv.Optional(..., default=...)` with sensible defaults.
- Call `await cg.register_component(var, config)` **before** attaching child sensors / platforms.
- For platforms, also call the matching `register_*` (e.g. `await sensor.new_sensor(...)`, `await climate.register_climate(var, config)`).

# C++ conventions

- Inherit from `Component` / `PollingComponent` plus the relevant base (`i2c::I2CDevice`, `climate::Climate`, ...).
- Setters on the class are small inline accessors. Do real work in `setup()` / `update()` / `loop()`.
- Use `ESP_LOGI` / `ESP_LOGW` etc. with a per-component tag.

# Debugging instrumentation

`ESP_LOGI("agent_dbg", ...)` lines are temporary. Strip or guard them before merging to `main`.

# Versioning

When a component reaches a stable point, tag it (e.g. `actron_modbus-v0.2.0`) so device configs can pin to it instead of tracking a branch.
